# Whoever owns a path is requested as reviewer automatically when a pull request changes it. With
# "Require review from Code Owners" switched on in the branch protection of main, their approval is
# also required. The last matching line wins, and an owner needs write access to the repository.
#
# To add people, put them after the path (a user: @name, a team: @EversIT/team-name). Examples:
#   /apps/backend/src/security/   @EversIT/security
#   /apps/frontend/               @EversIT/frontend
#   /apps/docs/                   @EversIT/docs

# Everything, until more specific owners are named below.
*                       @Optischa

# Changes that decide who may see what, how the database changes, and how releases are built. Listed
# separately so they stay with a named reviewer when the default above is widened to a team.
/apps/backend/src/security/   @Optischa
/apps/backend/src/identity/   @Optischa
/apps/backend/migrations/     @Optischa
/.github/                     @Optischa
/packages/docker/             @Optischa
/packages/deploy/                      @Optischa
